.TH SENTINELSCAN 1 "2026-08-04" "SentinelScan 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sentinelscan \- modular web security scanner
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sentinelscan
[\fITARGET\fR ...] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B sentinelscan
\-iL \fIFILE\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B sentinelscan
\-\-doctor | \-\-update\-db | \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sentinelscan
scans one or more web targets for misconfigurations: insecure HTTP headers,
TLS/SSL issues, cookie flaws, CORS vulnerabilities, DNS email-security gaps,
exposed ports, subdomain exposure, inconsistent header policy across a site,
and known-vulnerable software versions. Findings are scored and graded
(A+ through F) per target, and rendered as text, JSON, HTML, or SARIF.
.PP
Targets may be hostnames, URLs, CIDR ranges (expanded to individual hosts,
capped at 1024 per range), a host-list file (\fB\-iL\fR), or standard input
(pass \fB\-\fR as a target).
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Target Selection
.TP
.BI TARGET " ..."
Hostname, URL, or CIDR range to scan. Pass \fB\-\fR to read newline-separated
targets from stdin. May be repeated.
.TP
.BR \-iL ", " \-\-input\-list " " \fIFILE\fR
Read targets from \fIFILE\fR, one per line. Lines starting with \fB#\fR are
ignored. CIDR ranges are accepted.
.SS Module Selection
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-modules " " \fIMODULE\fR " [\fIMODULE\fR ...]"
Modules to run. Built-in:
.BR headers ", " ssl_tls ", " owasp ", " cookies ", " cors ", " dns ", "
.BR ports ", " subdomains ", " crawler ", " cve_fingerprint ", or " all
(default). Plugin modules (see \fB\-\-plugin\-dir\fR) are also selectable by
name once loaded.
.TP
.BR \-\-plugin\-dir " " \fIDIR\fR
Directory to load custom analyzer plugins from. Default:
\fI~/.config/sentinelscan/plugins\fR. See \fBPLUGINS\fR below.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-plugins
Disable plugin loading entirely for this run.
.SS Output
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format " " {text,json,html,sarif}
Output format. Default: \fBtext\fR. \fBsarif\fR emits SARIF 2.1.0 for GitHub
Code Scanning and similar tool-chains.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIFILE\fR
Write the report to \fIFILE\fR instead of stdout. Status/progress messages
always go to stderr regardless of this flag, so stdout stays clean for
piping when \fB\-o\fR is not used.
.TP
.BI \-\-severity " " LEVEL " [\fILEVEL\fR ...]"
Restrict output to the given severity levels:
.BR critical ", " high ", " medium ", " low ", " info .
Default: all.
.SS Timing & Concurrency
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-timing " " {0..5}
nmap-style timing template controlling default timeout and concurrency:
\fB0\fR paranoid (slowest, most polite) through \fB5\fR insane (fastest,
most parallel). Default: \fB3\fR (normal).
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " " SECONDS
Per-request timeout. Overrides the timing template's default (normally 10s)
without changing its concurrency.
.TP
.BI \-\-retries " " N
Retries on connection failure. Default: 2.
.TP
.BI \-\-crawl\-max\-pages " " N
Maximum pages the \fBcrawler\fR module visits. Default: 15.
.SS Authenticated Scanning
.TP
.BI \-H ", " \-\-header " " "'Name: Value'"
Add a custom HTTP header. May be repeated. Example:
\fB\-H 'Authorization: Bearer TOKEN'\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-cookie " " "'name=value; ...'"
Raw \fBCookie\fR header, for scanning behind an authenticated session.
.SS Network
.TP
.BI \-\-user\-agent " " STRING
Custom User-Agent string. Default: \fBSentinelScan/2.0 (Security Scanner)\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-follow\-redirects ", " \-\-no\-follow\-redirects
Follow HTTP redirects. Default: follow.
.SS CI/CD Gates
.TP
.B \-\-exit\-on\-critical
Exit with code 2 if any Critical-severity finding is present.
.TP
.BI \-\-score\-threshold " " SCORE
Exit with code 2 if the cumulative risk score exceeds \fISCORE\fR.
.SS Display
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI color in text output.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Verbose/debug output (also surfaces previously-silent internal probe
failures at debug level).
.SS Diagnostics & Maintenance
.TP
.B \-\-doctor
Report Python version, optional dependency availability (e.g. dnspython),
and config paths; exit 1 if anything needed is missing.
.TP
.B \-\-update\-db
Download the latest CVE signature dataset and install it as a user-level
override.
.TP
.BI \-\-update\-url " " URL
Custom source URL for \fB\-\-update\-db\fR (advanced).
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Scan completed; no CI/CD gate tripped (or \fB\-\-doctor\fR/\fB\-\-update\-db\fR succeeded).
.TP
.B 1
Usage or runtime error (bad target/CIDR, malformed \fB\-H\fR header, unknown
module, network failure). The scan did not complete.
.TP
.B 2
Scan completed successfully, but \fB\-\-exit\-on\-critical\fR and/or
\fB\-\-score\-threshold\fR tripped.
.SH PLUGINS
Drop a \fB*.py\fR file into the plugin directory exposing a module-level
\fBANALYZER\fR attribute (a \fBBaseAnalyzer\fR subclass with a unique
\fBname\fR) to add a custom check with no source changes. See
.B CONFIG.md
in the project documentation for the full interface.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sentinelscan/plugins/
Default plugin directory.
.TP
.I ~/.config/sentinelscan/cve_signatures.json
User-level CVE signature override, installed by \fB\-\-update\-db\fR.
.TP
.I ~/.config/sentinelscan/.disclaimer_shown
Marker file recording that the first-run authorized-use disclaimer has been shown.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SENTINELSCAN_SKIP_DISCLAIMER
Set to \fB1\fR to suppress the first-run disclaimer (e.g. in CI).
.TP
.B SENTINELSCAN_PLUGIN_DIR
Overrides the default plugin directory.
.TP
.B SENTINELSCAN_SIGNATURES_PATH
Overrides the default CVE signature override path.
.TP
.B SENTINELSCAN_CONFIG_DIR
Overrides the default config directory used for the disclaimer marker.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Basic scan, all modules, text output:
.RS
.EX
sentinelscan example.com
.EE
.RE
.PP
Specific modules, JSON to a file:
.RS
.EX
sentinelscan example.com \-m headers ssl_tls \-f json \-o results.json
.EE
.RE
.PP
CIDR range, aggressive timing, ports only:
.RS
.EX
sentinelscan 10.0.0.0/28 \-m ports \-\-timing 4
.EE
.RE
.PP
Authenticated scan, CI/CD gate:
.RS
.EX
sentinelscan example.com \-H 'Authorization: Bearer TOKEN' \-\-exit\-on\-critical
.EE
.RE
.SH LEGAL
.B sentinelscan
performs active probes (port connections, path enumeration, CORS/header
requests) against the target(s) given to it. Only scan systems you own or
have explicit written authorization to test. Unauthorized scanning may
violate computer-crime laws and the target's terms of service.
.PP
sentinelscan sends no telemetry. It contacts only: the scan target(s), crt.sh
(only when the
.B subdomains
module runs), and the URL given to
.B \-\-update\-url
(only when
.B \-\-update\-db
is used).
.SH AUTHOR
SentinelScan Contributors.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation: \fBREADME.md\fR, \fBUSAGE.md\fR, \fBCONFIG.md\fR,
\fBSECURITY.md\fR in the project source.
